 "notes": "Walking time is rounded to nearest (banker's rounding) instead of up, so footpaths whose length is not a multiple of 80 m can be one minute short (250 m -> 3, 200 m -> 2, 520 m -> 6, 40 m -> 0). The planner then catches departures the passenger cannot reach. Multiples of 80 m and lengths whose remainder rounds up anyway are unaffected (public tests use 80/160/240/400 m). Fixing the walk text in journeys only leaves the planner wrong.",
